# Kernel config fragment — Orange Pi Zero 2 (Allwinner H616, arm64) HEADLESS
# APPLIANCE. EXPERIMENTAL PLATFORM — see specs-orangepi-zero2/README.md: this
# board has NEVER been booted with an image from this repo. Every H616-specific
# symbol below is researched (web + kernel upstream source, incl. direct fetch
# of live mainline Linux/U-Boot source trees), NOT hardware-verified; treat
# every "verify" note as a real gap a reviewer must close before trusting this
# on real hardware.
#
# Applied on top of the chosen base defconfig by build-orangepi-zero2-stage4.sh
# using scripts/kconfig/merge_config.sh (the Frite/Jetson/Orange-Pi-5 convention
# — real Kconfig dependency-aware merging — NOT the x86/RPi5 `scripts/config
# --action` replay DSL). Three jobs:
#   1) Keep the SAME hardening posture as the rest of the fleet (SELinux LSM,
#      lockdown-friendly, audit) — the SELinux guard in the builder enforces it.
#   2) Enable H616 platform + Gigabit Ethernet (RTL8211F) + USB + storage so the
#      board actually boots and is reachable over the network.
#   3) LUKS2/dm-crypt (--encrypt-root) + the squashfs/overlay live-boot bits.
#
# ── DELIBERATELY ABSENT: NO GPU/DRM/display config, NO framebuffer console ────
# This is the ONE thing that makes this fragment different in KIND from every
# desktop-platform fragment in this repo (specs-frite, specs-orangepi5,
# specs-rpi5, specs-jetson all enable CONFIG_DRM_* + CONFIG_FB*): the H616's
# display engine (DE33) has ZERO mainline Linux DRM driver support as of the
# research behind this fragment (drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/ ships no DE33/H616
# driver; sun50i-h616.dtsi has NO &hdmi/&tcon/mixer nodes at all — confirmed by
# fetching the live upstream tree, not just reading claims about it). The
# board's physical Micro-HDMI 2.0a port is real hardware with no mainline
# software to drive it. Working HDMI exists ONLY via Allwinner's own
# never-upstreamed legacy-BSP kernel fork, or an Armbian community backport
# whose most recent activity (a Nov-2025-era out-of-tree DE33 patch series
# rebased onto Armbian's sunxi-6.12 kernel) caused BOOT FREEZES on this exact
# board (Orange Pi Zero 2/Zero 3) and a GPU-power-domain hang, walked back by a
# follow-up "remove the incomplete patch" bugfix PR — i.e. even the best
# available out-of-tree attempt is not stable. See specs-orangepi-zero2/README.md
# for the full research trail. DO NOT add CONFIG_DRM/CONFIG_DRM_SUN4I/
# CONFIG_FB*/CONFIG_FRAMEBUFFER_CONSOLE here by copy-paste habit from another
# platform's fragment — there is nothing for them to drive, and carrying the
# out-of-tree DE33 patches would mean maintaining an entire alternate kernel
# tree, a materially heavier commitment than any other platform in this repo.
#
# Format: standard .config fragment (CONFIG_FOO=y / # CONFIG_FOO is not set /
# CONFIG_FOO="string") — consumed by merge_config.sh, NOT by scripts/config.

# ── Allwinner sunxi platform (H616 shares this arm64 platform-select symbol
# with every other Allwinner SoC generation — H3/H5/H6/H616/...) ──────────────
CONFIG_ARCH_SUNXI=y

# ── eMMC / microSD (Allwinner sunxi MMC host controller) ───────────────────
# CONFIG_MMC_SUNXI is the mainline driver for Allwinner's SD/MMC host
# controller IP, documented for "allwinner,sun50i-h616-mmc" (VERIFIED against
# the LKDDB Kconfig database for this exact compatible string). This board has
# NO eMMC (microSD + a small onboard SPI NOR flash only — see the README's
# storage confidence notes) — CONFIG_MMC_SUNXI covers the microSD slot.
CONFIG_MMC=y
CONFIG_MMC_SUNXI=y

# ── SPI (the board's small onboard SPI NOR flash, and the SPI/UART header) ──
CONFIG_SPI=y
CONFIG_SPI_SUN6I=y
CONFIG_MTD=y
CONFIG_MTD_SPI_NOR=y

# ── USB (H616: 1x USB2 OTG + USB2 host ports via an onboard hub on some
# revisions; the physical full-size USB-A port + header pins) ─────────────────
# VERIFY the exact musb-vs-ehci/ohci split against the checked-out kernel tree
# and this board's devicetree — sunxi USB controller wiring has varied across
# Allwinner SoC generations; this is the current best-known mainline symbol set.
CONFIG_USB=y
CONFIG_USB_EHCI_HCD=y
CONFIG_USB_EHCI_HCD_PLATFORM=y
CONFIG_USB_OHCI_HCD=y
CONFIG_USB_OHCI_HCD_PLATFORM=y
CONFIG_USB_MUSB_HDRC=y
CONFIG_USB_MUSB_SUNXI=y
CONFIG_USB_STORAGE=y

# ── Networking: onboard Gigabit Ethernet (H616 EMAC0 + external RTL8211F PHY) ─
# The H616's internal EMAC controller cannot itself do gigabit; it is wired in
# RGMII mode to an EXTERNAL Realtek RTL8211F PHY chip for the real Gigabit
# link — this is the mainline pairing CONFIRMED against the current upstream
# devicetree (sun50i-h616-orangepi-zero2.dts ships a "allwinner,sun50i-h616-
# emac0" node + an RGMII-attached PHY). Both halves are mainline:
#   - CONFIG_DWMAC_SUN8I: the Allwinner sun8i/sun50i-family GMAC glue driver
#     (drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-sun8i.c) — CONFIRMED mainline.
#   - CONFIG_REALTEK_PHY: covers the RTL821x/RTL822x PHY family, including the
#     RTL8211F (drivers/net/phy/realtek/Kconfig — CONFIRMED mainline; the
#     Realtek PHY driver was refactored into its own drivers/net/phy/realtek/
#     subdirectory upstream, VERIFY the exact split still matches the checked-
#     out kernel tree, the Kconfig SYMBOL NAME itself, CONFIG_REALTEK_PHY, has
#     not changed).
CONFIG_NET=y
CONFIG_ETHERNET=y
CONFIG_NET_VENDOR_STMICRO=y
CONFIG_STMMAC_ETH=y
CONFIG_STMMAC_PLATFORM=y
CONFIG_DWMAC_SUN8I=y
CONFIG_PHYLIB=y
CONFIG_REALTEK_PHY=y

# ── WiFi/Bluetooth: DELIBERATELY NOT BUILT for the onboard radio ───────────
# The board's onboard radio is a Unisoc UWE5622 die packaged inside an
# Allwinner "AW859A" WiFi+BT combo module. CONFIRMED (research behind this
# fragment): there is NO mainline kernel.org driver for the UWE5622/AW859A at
# all — not even a rough/incomplete one (unlike Orange Pi 5's AP6275P, which at
# least has an upstream brcmfmac-class driver with known rough edges). The only
# working driver is Unisoc/Allwinner's own out-of-tree BSP module source. There
# is therefore NOTHING to gain by enabling CONFIG_CFG80211/CONFIG_MAC80211/a
# brcmfmac-class module here — no in-tree driver would ever bind to this chip.
# This board is headless + Ethernet-first anyway (see the README), so the
# onboard radio is simply left uncompiled rather than carrying dead module
# config for hardware nothing in mainline can drive. A USB WiFi dongle with its
# OWN mainline driver would still work via the arm64 base defconfig's own
# module set (unrelated to this fragment) — see harden_radios() in the builder
# for the generic cfg80211/mac80211/bluetooth/btusb modprobe-blacklist posture
# that applies to any such dongle, same as every other platform in this repo.

# ── Hardware crypto (ARMv8 Crypto Extensions on the H616's 4x Cortex-A53
# cores) — same core as Orange Pi 5's LITTLE cluster, so the same guaranteed
# accelerator applies here. ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
CONFIG_CRYPTO_AES_ARM64_CE_BLK=y

# ── LUKS2 root (dm-crypt) — --encrypt-root builds ──────────────────────────
# Same CONFIG_MD/BLK_DEV_DM/DM_CRYPT/CRYPTO_XTS/CRYPTO_AES pattern every other
# platform in this repo uses (x86/frite/rpi5/jetson/orangepi5). CONFIG_MD gates
# the whole drivers/md/Kconfig subtree that BLK_DEV_DM/DM_CRYPT depend on
# (directly or transitively) — without it, `make olddefconfig` silently drops
# them regardless of what's requested here.
CONFIG_MD=y
CONFIG_BLK_DEV_DM=y
CONFIG_DM_CRYPT=y
CONFIG_CRYPTO_XTS=y
CONFIG_CRYPTO_AES=y
CONFIG_CRYPTO_SHA512=y
CONFIG_CRYPTO_USER_API_HASH=y
CONFIG_CRYPTO_USER_API_SKCIPHER=y
# Disable hibernation — resume-from-disk bypasses LUKS2 disk encryption.
# Mirrors every other hardened-*.config in this repo.
# CONFIG_HIBERNATION is not set

# ── Hardening posture (MUST match the fleet; guarded by the builder) ───────
# SECURITY_NETWORK must come before SECURITY_SELINUX — selinux depends on it.
CONFIG_SECURITY=y
CONFIG_SECURITY_NETWORK=y
CONFIG_SECURITY_SELINUX=y
CONFIG_SECURITY_SELINUX_BOOTPARAM=y
CONFIG_SECURITY_YAMA=y
# Kernel lockdown (cmdline: lockdown=integrity). Mirrors specs-x86 + specs-rpi5; the
# 8 ARM boards used to ship neither the symbol nor the cmdline token. It SELECTS
# CONFIG_MODULE_SIG (Kconfig: `select MODULE_SIG if MODULES`), so every module this
# build installs is signed with the kernel's auto-generated key and an UNSIGNED or
# out-of-tree .ko is refused at runtime once lockdown=integrity is on. _EARLY makes
# lockdown run before every other LSM so the boot parameters are covered too.
CONFIG_SECURITY_LOCKDOWN_LSM=y
CONFIG_SECURITY_LOCKDOWN_LSM_EARLY=y
CONFIG_AUDIT=y
CONFIG_AUDITSYSCALL=y
CONFIG_BPF_SYSCALL=y
# `bpf` is deliberately NOT in this list. The kernel silently DROPS an LSM name
# whose module is absent — it prints a SHORTER "LSM: initializing lsm=..." and
# boots on — and CONFIG_BPF_LSM has never been set in ANY board fragment in this
# repo, nor are its Kconfig deps (BPF_JIT, BPF_EVENTS) enabled here. So the name
# only ever advertised a posture the running kernel did not have. yama IS real on
# this board (CONFIG_SECURITY_YAMA=y above). Re-add `bpf` only together with
# CONFIG_BPF_LSM + its deps AND a verified board build; the builder guard now
# derives the required CONFIG_* set from this very string and will fail without it.
# lockdown is listed FIRST so it activates before any other LSM (as on x86/rpi5).
CONFIG_LSM="lockdown,yama,selinux"
# ASLR / stack / slab hardening
CONFIG_RANDOMIZE_BASE=y
CONFIG_STACKPROTECTOR_STRONG=y
CONFIG_SLAB_FREELIST_HARDENED=y
CONFIG_SLAB_FREELIST_RANDOM=y
CONFIG_HARDENED_USERCOPY=y
CONFIG_FORTIFY_SOURCE=y

# ── tun + iptables (tailscale needs /dev/net/tun + nf) ─────────────────────
CONFIG_TUN=y
CONFIG_NETFILTER=y
CONFIG_NF_CONNTRACK=y
CONFIG_IP_NF_IPTABLES=y
CONFIG_NETFILTER_XTABLES=y

# ── Squashfs + overlay + loop (the LIVE flavor boots a squashfs) ───────────
# Same dmsquash-live boot design as Frite/RPi5/Orange-Pi-5: the LIVE/INSTALLER
# medium boots a dracut dmsquash-live initramfs that mounts LiveOS/squashfs.img
# read-only (loop + squashfs) and stacks a writable overlay = the ephemeral root.
CONFIG_SQUASHFS=y
CONFIG_SQUASHFS_XZ=y
CONFIG_OVERLAY_FS=y
CONFIG_BLK_DEV_LOOP=y
CONFIG_ISO9660_FS=y
CONFIG_DM_SNAPSHOT=y
CONFIG_BLK_DEV_RAM=y
CONFIG_DEVTMPFS=y
CONFIG_DEVTMPFS_MOUNT=y
CONFIG_TMPFS=y
CONFIG_TMPFS_POSIX_ACL=y
CONFIG_BLK_DEV_INITRD=y

# ── Serial console ONLY — no framebuffer console (see the header note) ────
# Plain 8250-family UART support for the debug UART (mainline devicetree:
# aliases { serial0 = &uart0; }; chosen { stdout-path = "serial0:115200n8"; } —
# CONFIRMED against the live upstream sun50i-h616-orangepi-zero.dtsi shared by
# this board). CONFIG_SERIAL_8250_DW is the DesignWare 8250 variant Allwinner's
# UART IP uses upstream.
CONFIG_SERIAL_8250=y
CONFIG_SERIAL_8250_CONSOLE=y
CONFIG_SERIAL_8250_DW=y
CONFIG_SERIAL_OF_PLATFORM=y
# Deliberately DISABLED: CONFIG_FB, CONFIG_FRAMEBUFFER_CONSOLE, CONFIG_DRM* —
# see the header. This board has no console beyond the serial UART. These
# MUST be explicit "is not set" directives, not just omitted from this
# fragment: the generic arm64 defconfig this builder starts from ships all
# three =y by default, and merge_config.sh only OVERRIDES a base default when
# a fragment says so explicitly — silently omitting a symbol leaves the base
# default untouched. (An earlier version of this fragment relied on omission
# alone, which left CONFIG_FRAMEBUFFER_CONSOLE=y in the final .config and
# tripped the builder's own post-olddefconfig guard on every real build.)
# CONFIG_DRM is not set
# CONFIG_FB is not set
# CONFIG_FRAMEBUFFER_CONSOLE is not set
